From: GoProSlowYo <68455785+goproslowyo@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 01:42:56 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 21/22] dndcp: Receive guest to host drags through a native
 drop target

A guest to host drag reaches the host through the detection window, an
Xwayland window that the compositor has to carry a Wayland drag into.
niri runs X clients through xwayland-satellite, which does not carry a
drag into X at all, so a drag out of the guest never reached the host
there, and each time the host asked, niri scrolled its view to the new
window.

Where the native drag source works, show the layer-shell overlays as a
drag destination instead. The overlay takes the drag as any Wayland
client would, picks text/uri-list, or else text, reads it through the
offer's pipe without blocking the main loop and within the V3 size
limit, and hands the bytes to the code that reads a GTK drop, so the
host sees the same messages. It accepts copy only. The host reads the
files after the drop, and a source that sees a move finish may delete
them first.

The overlay covers the output, so it must not keep what the host cannot
take. A drag with no usable type, a failed or oversized read, or data
the host was not told about goes on to the window under it, and the
pointer without a drag passes through to the windows under it. When the
host asks again while the overlay still holds the drag, the data goes to
the host again.

At the host's drop the button is released over the overlay, and the
overlay finishes the drop. If no drop has arrived 300 ms later, Escape
cancels the guest drag. Where it does not, as on sway, the overlay
stays until that drag drops on it or leaves, so the drag cannot drop on
a guest window behind it. If neither the drag nor the pointer reaches
the overlay after the moves that put the pointer on it, the plugin
falls back to the detection window for that drag. GNOME and X11 keep
the detection window.

Tested without the host, on sway 1.11 and niri 26.04, with a test drag
source driven through uinput: file and text drags read and dropped, a
held button, a drag that goes back into the guest and out again, a drag
the host cannot take, and a click on the overlay. File drags to the
host were tested by hand on Plasma 6.7.5 and sway 1.11. On Plasma the
host kept the button down after the drop, and Escape cancelled the
guest drag.
